('4b82b60c-074d-5158-8647-dfd13c078078', $c$js-mfr-003$c$, $c$single_choice$c$, $c$Why does this print undefined?$c$, $c${"code":"const tally = ['a', 'b', 'a'].reduce((acc, ch) => {\n  acc[ch] = (acc[ch] ?? 0) + 1;\n}, {});\nconsole.log(tally);","options":["The callback never returns the accumulator","The initial value should be an array","?? cannot be used with objects","reduce does not support string arrays"]}$c$::jsonb, $c$The callback's return value becomes the next accumulator.$c$, 2, 1, 'published', array[$c$reduce$c$, $c$return$c$]::text[]),
