('39bfdde1-989b-53cb-b069-45c437bf7765', $c$js-debug-001$c$, $c$single_choice$c$, $c$Given this stack trace, where should you look first?$c$, $c${"code":"TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'value')\n    at readTotal (form.js:8:22)\n    at submit (form.js:30:14)\n    at HTMLFormElement.<anonymous> (form.js:41:3)","options":["form.js line 8, inside readTotal","form.js line 41, where the listener is attached","form.js line 30, inside submit","The browser's internal code"]}$c$::jsonb, $c$The top frame is where the error was thrown.$c$, 1, 1, 'published', array[$c$stack-trace$c$]::text[]),
('08c093f6-d6fd-5e85-aa3c-8498cabdaa31', $c$js-debug-002$c$, $c$single_choice$c$, $c$What is a likely reason the console shows { count: 2 } for the first log?$c$, $c${"code":"const state = { count: 1 };\nconsole.log(state);\nstate.count = 2;","options":["The console shows a live reference that is expanded after the mutation","console.log is asynchronous and ran after the assignment","Objects are always logged with their final value","The assignment ran before the log because of hoisting"]}$c$::jsonb, $c$Logged objects are references; expanding later shows the current state.$c$, 1, 1, 'published', array[$c$console$c$, $c$live-references$c$]::text[]),
